From 887ef29c20ecee086df29c3838473de325d893ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:40:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] buildroot: re-wire the shared RNSBox packages into
 package/Config.in

Patch 0024 (de-vendoring) removed the four source lines together with
the vendored package copies, but the shared packages that build.sh
syncs from <repo>/package/ still need to be SOURCED for kconfig to see
them - without the lines the defconfig's BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_RNS et al
are silently dropped and the rootfs ships without rnsd or the portal.
Append the sources at the end of package/Config.in (the vendored
placement mid-file is gone with 0024).
---
 buildroot/package/Config.in | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/buildroot/package/Config.in b/buildroot/package/Config.in
index f800bcf94..cfcf514b7 100644
--- a/buildroot/package/Config.in
+++ b/buildroot/package/Config.in
@@ -2818,3 +2818,8 @@ endmenu
 
 
 endmenu
+	# RNSBox shared packages (synced from <repo>/package/ by build.sh)
+	source "package/python-rns/Config.in"
+	source "package/python-lxmf/Config.in"
+	source "package/python-nomadnet/Config.in"
+	source "package/rnsbox-portal/Config.in"
-- 
2.43.0

